{
  "about": "What spell_core doesn't have yet of the core's method list (src/core/core.declarations.json5), by the JavaScript name, grouped by why.  Read by tests/py/core/tests/test_core_declarations.py, and by the core reference page (guides/targets/core-reference.html).  Take a name out as it's ported.",
  "groups": [
    {
      "why": "The steps around a server's action (epic data P50):  before, while, around and when it fails, the app's own for every server call, and an id read first;  Python's places call no server's actions yet",
      "names": ["addActionHook", "addServerFailureStep", "passTheError", "errorIs", "savedThingOrMissing"]
    },
    {
      "why": "A site's pages by address (epic mockup P2):  a site runs in the browser's Run first;  Python's pages come later",
      "names": ["siteHost", "showSitePart", "closeSitePart", "siteAddressOf", "SiteBase", "savedIdOf", "projectFolder", "addressOfFile"]
    },
    {
      "why": "A value that waits, on a page:  Python sends its page with its values (answer_of(), answer_now()), so it has no \"…\" to show (epic language P12)",
      "names": ["waitedValue", "waitedValueKeyFor", "whileWaiting"]
    },
    {
      "why": "choose's dialog on a page (epic language P66):  Python's choose() names its rows itself, and asks its page for this",
      "names": ["choosePositions"]
    },
    {
      "why": "The person menu, drawn on a page (epic atmosphere T56):  a program in Python has no toolbar of its own to put it in yet",
      "names": ["signInMenu"]
    },
    {
      "why": "Actions run by a person's keys, clicks and menus (epic elemental-spell P10):  a page's, not yet Python's",
      "names": [
        "runAction",
        "runPressed",
        "pressed",
        "holdWhile",
        "runningAction",
        "actionFinishing",
        "takesEvent",
        "isActionEnabled",
        "isActionSelected",
        "actionTitle",
        "useTitles",
        "onActionRun",
        "runShortcut",
        "menuOf",
        "menuBarOf",
        "actionOf",
        "menuItemsOf"
      ]
    },
    {
      "why": "What people may do to a thing on the page, drag, click, select, drop on it (epic debut P27):  a page's, not yet Python's",
      "names": ["isAble"]
    },
    {
      "why": "Pauses and events (P11):  Python's runtime hasn't needed these",
      "names": [
        "forEachSequential",
        "DEBUG_RUNTIME",
        "DEBUG_PROCESSES",
        "clearRuntime"
      ]
    },
    {
      "why": "A browser's only:  a view's own element (<solitaire-card>), a page's markup, its shadow root",
      "names": [
        "elementDefiner",
        "beforeMove",
        "defineElement",
        "elementFor",
        "elementApiOf",
        "thingFor",
        "appLayout",
        "domRoot",
        "projectSheet",
        "uiDefaults",
        "giveDefaults",
        "handDefaultsTo",
        "listDrawn",
        "listShown",
        "useElement",
        "elementClassOf",
        "uiElementOf",
        "css"
      ]
    },
    {
      "why": "Sounds and videos (epic data T145, language P65):  a page's speakers and screen, played from a person's click;  a Python program's page would play them, not the program",
      "names": [
        "media",
        "mediaNamed",
        "pause",
        "resume",
        "stopAll",
        "isPlaying",
        "isDone",
        "mediaLength",
        "drawMedia"
      ]
    },
    {
      "why": "The mouse and keys (epic elemental-spell P9):  a Python program's page sends them to its things",
      "names": ["input"]
    },
    {
      "why": "A page's drag handlers (epic outline-spell P28):  the page calls them;  a Python program's page sends them to its things, as `start_while()` and `end_while()`",
      "names": [
        "remote",
        "runHandler",
        "moveBefore",
        "startWhile",
        "endWhile"
      ]
    },
    {
      "why": "A recompile keeping the last run's things (epic drawable-thing P16, P17):  the page's runners only;  a Python program never keeps them",
      "names": [
        "isCarryingOver",
        "carryOver",
        "drawAgain",
        "drawPart",
        "keptTopLevel",
        "loadOverRunning",
        "takeNewClasses",
        "carryProblems"
      ]
    },
    {
      "why": "An element's id on the page (epic drawable-thing P18):  the page's own javascript gives it, never the program",
      "names": [
        "elementIdFor"
      ]
    },
    {
      "why": "What the lookups search (epic people-and-orgs P9):  Python's take what they search on each call, thing_for_reference(reference, things, kept)",
      "names": [
        "searchThings"
      ]
    },
    {
      "why": "Running a project's tests from a runner (epic spanish, Card Checks and Test Results):  spell test and the VS Code runner's Run Tests, on the JavaScript core;  Python's tests run under pytest",
      "names": [
        "testResults",
        "runTests"
      ]
    },
    {
      "why": "Remembered props (epic prefs-and-undo P8):  kept in the person's preferences, in a browser or on the page server;  a Python program keeps none yet",
      "names": [
        "remember"
      ]
    },
    {
      "why": "Not decided yet:  a word of Python's own, a browser's only, or ported when a program needs it",
      "names": [
        "doNothing",
        "flush",
        "TYPE_NAME_CONVERSIONS",
        "IS_OF_TYPE_SPECIALS",
        "get",
        "set",
        "absoluteValue",
        "repeat",
        "doubleQuote",
        "getPath",
        "setPath",
        "splitPath"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
